  <section id="vosstanovlenie">
    <h2>Recovery</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right after surgery</strong> you can hold light objects — a mug, a spoon, a phone. For the first days keep the hand raised to reduce swelling.</li>
      <li><strong>For the first 2 weeks</strong> do not lean on the palm or lift anything heavy with that hand.</li>
      <li><strong>Stitches</strong> are removed on day 10–14. Until then keep the hand dry and treat the wound with an antiseptic.</li>
      <li><strong>Exercises</strong> start once the wound has healed — about 10–14 days after surgery. They help restore mobility and sensation faster. <a href="#uprazhneniya">Five hand exercises</a> are above in this article.</li>
      <li><strong>Sensation and strength</strong> return gradually: over several weeks to several months. The shorter the compression, the faster and fuller the recovery.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Returning to work</h3>
    <p>Most people return to work in 2–3 weeks. At first it is important not to press on the wrist. If you work at a computer a lot, wear a splint, put a soft pad under the wrist, choose a comfortable mouse — for example a vertical one — and watch your grip so the hand does not rest on the operated area.</p>
    <figure class="photo-fig narrow">
      <img src="/media/cases/carpal-3-months.webp" alt="Palm 3 months after carpal tunnel surgery: the scar is hard to see" width="900" height="995" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>The hand 3 months after surgery. The wound has healed and the scar is hard to see.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="srochno" slot="urgent">
    <h2>When to seek urgent help</h2>
    <div class="callout alert">
      <p>Carpal tunnel syndrome develops gradually. If weakness or numbness of the arm appears <strong>suddenly</strong>, especially with speech problems, a drooping face or weakness of the leg on the same side, it may be a stroke. <strong>Call emergency services immediately (112; 103 in Russia).</strong></p>
      <p>If after a cut or injury your fingers stop obeying or lose sensation, see a surgeon within days: an injured nerve is best repaired as early as possible.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
